cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "Parametric Multimodal User Memory: Storing What Captions Cannot Carry"
abstract: >-
  A personalized AI agent needs a user memory. Today that memory is almost
  always text, which captures the captionable half of a person but silently
  drops the perceptual half — how a voice sounds, how a face reads across age
  and lighting. We introduce parametric multimodal user memory: the agent
  stores each perception directly as a row in a small per-modality bank
  attached to a frozen language model and recalls it by attention at
  generation time, with no captioning step. On PerceptMem, a benchmark
  spanning faces, voices, painter style, room acoustics, and tone of voice,
  the mechanism beats the strongest text-free baseline because it measures
  similarity in the model's own representation space rather than the encoder's.
